<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>104 / 104</strong><span>Core contexts completed · 6,320-context catalog remains incomplete</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>14 + 14</strong><span>Frozen core and retained historical metric roles</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>46</strong><span>Recovered native original target rows · 8 games · no new dashboard issuance</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>420 / 403</strong><span>Men / women in latest B003 current-season replay</span></div></div>
<div class="notice"><strong>Research completion and production promotion are separate.</strong><p>B062 ended with resource-deferred work preserved. The core study completed, while the full research catalog and rolling-champion terminal closure remain incomplete. A physical fit-accounting failure means the terminal aggregate does not establish an exact total of new fits. B063 owner execution and 12-core performance still require owner-runtime evidence.</p><p>Current outcomes did not select the completed-season research roles. These development-exposed roles have no automatic production promotion or independent confirmation.</p></div>
<section id="terminal-roles"><h2>Champions by objective</h2><p class="sub">2024–25 and 2025–26 are the frozen evaluation seasons. “Research champion” describes the registered historical selection, not a universally superior or production-promoted model. Public aliases preserve the private recipe boundary. Higher accuracy is better; lower loss, Brier and point error are better.</p><div class="controls"><label>Research catalog<select id="terminal-role-kind"><option value="frozen_core_roles">Frozen core · 14 selected roles</option><option value="retained_historical_metric_roles">Retained historical · 14 roles</option></select></label><label>League<select id="terminal-role-league"><option value="all">Men and women</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></label></div><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-role-table"><thead><tr><th>League</th><th>Target / objective</th><th>Selected model alias / family</th><th>Value</th><th>Games</th><th>Qualification</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="fine">The core selection cutoff was October 1, 2026. The observed 14-role table is exposed development evidence; displayed intervals, where retained, are descriptive and are not selection-adjusted confirmation.</p></section>
<section><h2>Retained models still matter</h2><p class="sub">The retained historical roles have numerically better reported values on 12 of 14 objectives. The new core is better on women’s accuracy and margin MAE. These are two registered research universes with equal league support; this display does not calculate paired cross-study uncertainty or select a production replacement. This evidence supports preserving and re-evaluating the legacy work.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-overlap-table"><thead><tr><th>League / objective</th><th>Retained role</th><th>New core role</th><th>Numerically better</th><th>Support</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="terminal-season"><h2>Same-model metrics, season by season</h2><p class="sub">All 50 saved selected-model rows remain available. A pooled leader does not imply that it leads every season or metric. The 2026–27 rows are current monitoring or reconstruction, not a new untouched holdout. Counts are eligible scored observations, not certified official season totals.</p><h3>Best values within the inspected selected-model subset</h3><p class="sub">These four season/league summaries compare the saved selected candidates on exact equal target cohorts. They are not a search of the unfinished full catalog. Each cell retains the model alias so that different objectives cannot be mistaken for one model.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-season-best"><thead><tr><th>Season / league</th><th>N</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Log loss</th><th>Brier</th><th>Margin MAE</th><th>Margin RMSE</th><th>Total MAE</th><th>Total RMSE</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h3>Inspect each saved candidate</h3><div class="controls"><label>Season<select id="terminal-season-filter"><option value="all">All saved seasons</option><option value="2025">2024–25 · frozen</option><option value="2026">2025–26 · frozen</option><option value="2027">2026–27 · monitoring</option></select></label><label>League<select id="terminal-season-league"><option value="all">Men and women</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></label><label>Target<select id="terminal-season-target"><option value="all">All targets</option><option value="win">Win probability</option><option value="margin">Home margin</option><option value="total">Total points</option></select></label></div><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-season-table"><thead><tr><th>Season / league</th><th>Model alias / target</th><th>N</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Log loss</th><th>Brier</th><th>MAE</th><th>RMSE</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="terminal-current"><h2>2026–27 monitoring</h2><p class="sub">B003 is retained and replayed without changing its saved weights. Its new 420-game men’s and 403-game women’s samples extend the earlier 415/399 replay; earlier scores remain in the dated archive below. Replay results and original issued performance are not combined.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-b003-table"><thead><tr><th>League / target</th><th>N</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Log loss</th><th>Brier</th><th>MAE</th><th>RMSE</th><th>Calibration</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h3>Descriptive current metric leaders</h3><p class="sub">These 14 rows describe observed current results. Current outcomes do not grant selection or promotion authority. Different objectives can have different leaders; the exact tied public aliases are retained.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-current-table"><thead><tr><th>League</th><th>Target / metric</th><th>Observed public aliases</th><th>Value</th><th>N</th><th>Evidence mode</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="terminal-issues"><h2>Original issues recovered from B062</h2><p class="sub">46 selected native model or selected blend-component target rows cover eight games. Each immutable issue body and original server-before-cutoff timestamp was reopened. Component forecasts do not become an invented ensemble forecast. These games were scheduled November 12 at 02:00 or 02:30 UTC; results have not been refreshed and they are not labeled “upcoming now.”</p><div id="terminal-issue-cards" class="issue-list"></div><p class="fine">Original issuance labels can describe a pending commit inside a row; the independent immutable object readback establishes the subsequently verified server commit. The audit did not reread every original model/input body and is not certification of every forecast write in the whole run.</p></section>
<section id="terminal-games"><h2>Every observed game, with honest gaps</h2><p class="sub">The saved display contains 3,425 source game/time identities as of November 11, 22:28 UTC. It includes unresolved identities and unverified phase records; it is not a certified complete official schedule. Future unissued values are blank. Original event-time identities are preserved even when a later schedule changes.</p><div class="controls"><label>Forecast view<select id="terminal-game-mode"><option value="recovered_native_original">Recovered native original issues</option><option value="preserved_prior_original">Earlier preserved original issues</option><option value="original_reference">B003 original-model replay</option><option value="preserved_role">Retained historical-role replay</option><option value="additional_role">Additional historical-role replay</option></select></label><label>League<select id="terminal-game-league"><option value="all">Men and women</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></label><label>Coverage<select id="terminal-game-state"><option value="with">Has output in this view</option><option value="all">All observed records</option><option value="missing">No output in this view</option><option value="completed">Observed completed</option><option value="after">After saved display cutoff</option><option value="tbd">Unknown / TBD time</option></select></label><label>Team or source game ID<input id="terminal-game-search" type="search" placeholder="Search all saved records"></label><button id="terminal-game-reset">Reset</button><button id="terminal-game-download">Export filtered CSV</button></div><p class="statusline" id="terminal-game-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-game-table"><thead><tr><th>League / game</th><th>Original / source time UTC</th><th>Home win</th><th>Home margin</th><th>Total</th><th>Source / output state</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class="pager"><button id="terminal-game-prev">Previous</button><span id="terminal-game-page"></span><button id="terminal-game-next">Next</button></div><details id="terminal-game-detail-box"><summary>Selected game evidence and original clocks</summary><pre id="terminal-game-detail">Choose “Inspect” on a game.</pre></details><p class="fine">The earlier preserved view retains 96 target rows across 32 games; two changed-tip identities remain unscored. Another provisional 186-target B032 summary match is not published as additional original forecasts because exact immutable body binding was not reopened. Saved headline metrics use full precision; displayed probabilities and points are rounded only for reporting.</p></section>
<section id="terminal-markets"><h2>Market comparisons require matched evidence</h2><div class="two"><div class="card"><h3>B003 vs Polymarket international</h3><p>338 matched men’s win-probability observations, 2026–27. Both model and quote evidence are retrospective reconstructions. Higher accuracy and lower probability error favor different sides.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table id="terminal-market-match"><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>B003</th><th>Provider</th><th>Model minus provider</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="fine">Only three week blocks are available; the four-block minimum was not met, so no uncertainty interval or statistically confirmed superiority is claimed.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Provider coverage</h3><div id="terminal-provider-coverage"></div><p class="fine">Maximum matching support in one saved comparison is shown. Counts across candidate comparisons are not unique games. Missing evidence is not zero error. Point means are not inferred from binary total or spread markets.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="terminal-promotion"><h2>What is good enough for promotion?</h2><p class="sub">There is no universal accuracy or log-loss pass mark. Register the target, primary metric, matched support, season/week clustering, confidence and multiplicity policy, calibration guardrails, stability, coverage, resource cost and rollback before observing a new cohort. Compare the same events, target, horizon and source eligibility. Keep win probability, expected home margin, expected total/final score and calibrated cover probability as separate targets, with score/margin/total coherence and explicit push/overtime rules.</p><div class="two"><div class="card"><h3>Historical qualification is a research gate</h3><p>The recovered role code requires at least 500 pooled games, 100 in each frozen season and eight season/week clusters. Those requirements and the saved multiplicity method are not universal promotion thresholds. Development-exposed best scores require independent confirmation and calibration/stability review.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Prospective evidence starts after registration</h3><p>Monitoring current outcomes cannot rewrite old forecasts or turn a post-observation policy into an independent prospective test. New prospective credit begins only after registration and actual durable issuance. A new score, model fit or website deployment alone does not promote a model.</p></div></div></section>
<section><h2>Evidence and continuation</h2><p class="sub">This report adds authenticated terminal evidence without fitting models, acquiring market data, issuing predictions or changing champions operationally. All older published data remains in the dated view below. Full rolling-champion terminal completion and B063 owner parallel execution remain unverified.</p><details><summary>Source hashes, coverage and terminal status</summary><pre id="terminal-provenance"></pre></details></section>
<footer>Research analysis only. Source observation, original issuance, replay, software publication and website deployment are separate events. No wagering execution is provided.</footer>
